nce of aberrant and normal bands. These sequence analyses showed deletion of the <italic>EGFR</italic> gene in PC9.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="92-6602559f6"/></fig><fig id="fig7"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>Multicolour FISH analyses of PC9 (<bold>A</bold>) and PC9/f14 (<bold>B</bold>). Chromosome numbers of PC9 and PC9/f14 are 61 and 60, respectively. Common aberrant chromosomes are eight.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="92-6602559f7"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title"><italic>In vitro</italic> growth-inhibitory activity of gefitinib on NSCLC cell lines in the MTT assay</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Cell line</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Cell type</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>IC<sub>50</sub> (<italic>&#x003bc;</italic><sc>M</sc>)</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">PC9</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Adenocarcinoma</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">2.0 &#x000d7; 10<sup>&#x02212;3</sup></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">PC9/f9</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Highly metastatic subpopulation of PC9</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x0003e;20</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">PC9/f14</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Highly metastatic subpopulation of PC9</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">19</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">A549</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Adenocarcinoma</td><td align=